# Supabase (browser-safe key only — never commit service role / secret key)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# Publishable (sb_publishable_...) or legacy anon JWT (eyJ...) from Settings → API Keys
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key

# Optional build label (runtime uses hostname: web_localhost vs web_github_pages)
# VITE_PLATFORM=web_github_pages

# Optional — defaults to package version at build time if unset
# VITE_GAME_VERSION=0.0.0

# --- GitHub Pages (CI) ---
# Copy .env values into the repo as Actions secrets (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# Pushes to `main` run `.github/workflows/deploy-github-pages.yml` and deploy `dist/` to `gh-pages`.
# Local `npm run deploy` uses your `.env` during `npm run build`, or copy
# `public/escape-analytics.json.example` → `public/escape-analytics.json`.
# Platform in segments is detected from hostname (localhost vs *.github.io).

# --- Player accounts (migration 005) ---
# Run `supabase/migrations/005_escape_accounts.sql` in the SQL editor (after 001–004).
# If register fails with gen_salt(unknown, integer), run `007_escape_accounts_pgcrypto_fix.sql`.
# If register fails with "subquery must return only one column", run `008_escape_accounts_return_fix.sql`.
# If UUID errors show a full "(uuid,...)" row string, run `009_escape_accounts_jsonb_returns.sql` and clear site data / log out.
# Minimalist achievement column: `010_escape_accounts_minimalist.sql`.
# Google OAuth username picker: `011_escape_oauth_choose_username.sql`.
# RPCs: escape_register_account, escape_login_account, escape_get_account,
#       escape_record_run_started, escape_record_segment_progress.
# Passwords are bcrypt-hashed server-side; clients only receive `escape_accounts_public` rows.
# Google sign-in (required for “Continue with Google”; run migration 006):
#   1. Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client (Web).
#      - Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 and your deployed game URL
#      - Authorized redirect URI: https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   2. Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google → Enable → paste Client ID + Secret → Save
#   3. Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration:
#      - Site URL: your game URL (e.g. http://localhost:5173/ or https://user.github.io/Escape/)
#      - Redirect URLs: same origins as above (wildcard ok for localhost)
# If Google is not enabled, the game shows: “Unsupported provider: provider is not enabled”.
